From: Paul Gofman <pgofman@codeweavers.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: Answer app package lookups from the registry.

Adapted for CrossOver 26.3 from gauthierpiarrette/highball-engine
commit e13247c012c6d71fb705406d31b714bfea714cfc (patch 0024), which
takes these from Proton (ValveSoftware/wine, Paul Gofman):
GetPackagesByPackageFamily() 7b4037421ea8c407837548f0f9a1b5ca5e2b1226,
GetPackagePath() 8089c27dae7b4f47893cf2b29d6e8bbf7b1555db,
PackageFullNameFromId() c18ebc392d1eb3f18f8b44034d088678841112b8 and
the wine.inf package repository 09fbb2c010216c304c2e8cf2b145d43002c4b082.
Changed here: PackageFullNameFromId() accepts a NULL resource id as
WineHQ's ef6c413c68 does, the missing-key message is a warning, and
two messages gain their newline. A downstream port; WineHQ has
PackageFullNameFromId() since 11.18 (ef6c413c68) and still stubs the
other two.

GetPackagesByPackageFamily() was a stub that answered success with
zero packages, and a program that waits for the Visual C++ libraries
framework package (Microsoft.VCLibs.140.00_8wekyb3d8bbwe) never got
past its start (Wine bug 55397). It now lists the packages registered
under HKLM\Software\Classes\Local Settings\Software\Microsoft\Windows\
CurrentVersion\AppModel\PackageRepository\Packages, GetPackagePath()
reads a package's Path there, and PackageFullNameFromId() builds the
full name they need. wine.inf registers the VCLibs framework package
for each architecture, pointing at system32 (syswow64 for WoW64), as
Proton does; the entries do not replace existing values.

